WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.668
Hi, I'm David Hornsby.

00:00:01.668 --> 00:00:02.460
I'm Ashly Burch.

00:00:02.460 --> 00:00:03.461
-I'm Daniel Pudi.

00:00:03.461 --> 00:00:05.839
And we're here to
talk about our first time.

00:00:05.839 --> 00:00:06.756
-Directing.
-Directing.

00:00:06.756 --> 00:00:07.632
-Yes, directing. I’m sorry. Is that not clear?

00:00:07.632 --> 00:00:08.925
-Yeah. Directing.
-Directing.

00:00:08.925 --> 00:00:14.222
(Rock music)

00:00:14.222 --> 00:00:16.266
-I definitely had
moments where I was like,

00:00:16.266 --> 00:00:18.393
“Why do I want to
cut everything that I'm in?”

00:00:18.393 --> 00:00:21.354
Down to as
minimal as possible.

00:00:21.354 --> 00:00:22.981
And I was like, “Oh, it’s just
because I'm an actor.”

00:00:22.981 --> 00:00:25.316
It's not that hard...

00:00:25.316 --> 00:00:25.817
...Right?

00:00:25.817 --> 00:00:27.569
It's not that hard.
You just do your thing,

00:00:27.569 --> 00:00:29.446
and then you're
like, “A’ight. We good?

00:00:29.446 --> 00:00:30.739
Okay. Let’s move on.”

00:00:30.739 --> 00:00:32.240
I didn't even
yell, “Action” or “Cut”.

00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:33.867
I don’t think I- I-
-I don’t think I did once either.

00:00:33.867 --> 00:00:36.661
-one time yell ‘Action’ or ‘Cut’
-Really, you need to act like it’s more involved.

00:00:36.661 --> 00:00:38.371
-Oh. Oh, shoot.
-You gotta- yeah. Maybe act like-

00:00:38.371 --> 00:00:41.249
-Guys, this is very difficult stuff.
-Yeah, it requires some finesse.

00:00:41.249 --> 00:00:43.793
-I'll tell the camera people here.

00:00:43.793 --> 00:00:46.046
You guys don't
know how hard it is.

00:00:46.046 --> 00:00:48.423
-Mr. Brittlesbee is very busy.
If you're mentally ill,

00:00:48.423 --> 00:00:50.508
I'd be more than happy to
drive you to a nearby asylum.

00:00:50.508 --> 00:00:51.509
-Jo, please.

00:00:51.509 --> 00:00:53.970
What did Rob
and Megan say to you,

00:00:53.970 --> 00:00:55.513
in terms of
advice for directing?

00:00:55.764 --> 00:00:56.556
-Nothing.

00:00:56.556 --> 00:00:58.224
(Laughing)

00:00:58.224 --> 00:00:59.434
Uh... “Don’t screw it up!”

00:00:59.434 --> 00:00:59.976
No, I don't know.

00:00:59.976 --> 00:01:01.144
They were just
like, “You'll be fine.”

00:01:01.144 --> 00:01:02.312
-Yeah.
(Laughter)

00:01:02.312 --> 00:01:04.147
Rob said, “Come with a plan,

00:01:04.147 --> 00:01:05.356
be prepared to throw it out.”

00:01:05.356 --> 00:01:08.651
-If your gut is
right 51% of the time,

00:01:08.651 --> 00:01:09.527
that's a good gut.

00:01:09.527 --> 00:01:12.697
-Megan said, “Babysit,
be a good babysitter.”

00:01:12.697 --> 00:01:14.032
-Who was she talking about?

00:01:14.032 --> 00:01:15.200
(Laughter)

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:16.659
-But it was good. I
feel like I learned a lot.

00:01:16.659 --> 00:01:19.621
It was a nice way to, like,
really appreciate and see the-

00:01:19.621 --> 00:01:21.498
you know, how much
 goes into into the show.

00:01:21.498 --> 00:01:22.373
What about you?

00:01:23.249 --> 00:01:24.167
-Didn't say anything.

00:01:24.167 --> 00:01:25.627
(Laughing)

00:01:25.627 --> 00:01:27.087
They said, “Uh, we're leaving.

00:01:27.087 --> 00:01:29.339
If you got this,
then we're gonna go home.”

00:01:29.339 --> 00:01:30.423
And I was like,
“Yeah, that's fine.

00:01:30.423 --> 00:01:32.217
That’s fair. That’s fair. Go.”

00:01:32.217 --> 00:01:34.219
How do I look?
Big time Hollywood producer?

00:01:34.636 --> 00:01:36.471
More like, big time
Hollywood pedophile.

00:01:36.471 --> 00:01:38.014
-What are you the most
proud of from your episode?

00:01:38.014 --> 00:01:39.349
That it’s complete.

00:01:39.349 --> 00:01:41.392
-I hope!  For sure.
-That my episode is done.

00:01:41.392 --> 00:01:42.644
I'm so proud of that.

00:01:42.644 --> 00:01:44.104
-I think I'm
gonna echo that with,

00:01:44.104 --> 00:01:46.356
just getting it covered.
I think that there were

00:01:46.356 --> 00:01:47.315
a few scenes where I was like,

00:01:47.315 --> 00:01:49.400
“I just hope we
covered it all,” you know?

00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:51.236
Like, you were in
a great scene with Rob

00:01:51.236 --> 00:01:52.737
where you were
both improv-ing a lot about,

00:01:52.737 --> 00:01:55.073
you know, Superman,
and flying, and shoe size.

00:01:55.073 --> 00:01:57.117
-And would you
like to know the size?

00:01:57.117 --> 00:01:57.826
13.

00:01:57.826 --> 00:01:58.743
Let me see that.

00:01:58.743 --> 00:01:59.619
Let me see that the-

00:01:59.619 --> 00:02:00.954
oh, that is so sad.
-Now it’s too late.

00:02:00.954 --> 00:02:02.413
-I was like,
“I hope we got it all.”

00:02:02.413 --> 00:02:02.997
-Mm.
-Y’know?

00:02:02.997 --> 00:02:05.708
And I think we did.
And that felt nice.

00:02:05.708 --> 00:02:07.961
When I went and saw
with- with Josh, the editor,

00:02:07.961 --> 00:02:09.796
And being like, “Okay,
good. It cuts together.”

00:02:09.796 --> 00:02:11.506
-I think I'm the most proud

00:02:11.506 --> 00:02:14.175
that during my
episode, the crew wasn’t like:

00:02:14.175 --> 00:02:16.553
(Laughter)

00:02:16.553 --> 00:02:17.345
-Yeah.

00:02:17.345 --> 00:02:18.680
All right, yeah, actor directing...

00:02:18.680 --> 00:02:19.514
Cool, cool, cool.

00:02:19.514 --> 00:02:20.473
-Yeah.
-I mean, like...

00:02:20.473 --> 00:02:21.558
-Did anything surprise you

00:02:21.558 --> 00:02:22.600
when you
were, like, doing it?

00:02:22.600 --> 00:02:26.312
-I was surprised that
I wasn't a total mess.

00:02:26.312 --> 00:02:27.897
Honestly!
-You weren’t. You were really great.

00:02:27.897 --> 00:02:29.649
Confident. Great. It was awesome.
-Yeah! You faked it-

00:02:29.649 --> 00:02:31.192
You faked it very well.

00:02:31.943 --> 00:02:32.569
-I'm gonna-

00:02:32.569 --> 00:02:34.362
I'm gonna be a writer, Brad.

00:02:34.362 --> 00:02:35.113
-Ugh. Yuck.

00:02:35.113 --> 00:02:36.614
-How did you find
giving actors notes?

00:02:36.614 --> 00:02:37.699
What's the-

00:02:37.699 --> 00:02:39.409
what's a nice way to say

00:02:39.409 --> 00:02:41.244
you want
something different?

00:02:41.995 --> 00:02:42.620
-That's a good question.

00:02:42.620 --> 00:02:45.623
I realized while I
was directing that...

00:02:46.541 --> 00:02:48.835
I have to use less words, you know?

00:02:48.835 --> 00:02:51.546
-Again, not to just blow
smoke up everyone’s a**.

00:02:51.546 --> 00:02:53.965
But I never was
in the position where

00:02:53.965 --> 00:02:55.884
I was like, “Ooh.
That just didn't work.”

00:02:55.884 --> 00:02:59.012
It was more like,
“Oh, it would be fun to try this.”

00:02:59.012 --> 00:03:00.722
For Imani, for example,

00:03:00.722 --> 00:03:02.974
she had a scene
with Rob and Charlotte,

00:03:02.974 --> 00:03:05.560
and to have a
moment of going up to her

00:03:05.560 --> 00:03:07.020
and being like,
“You don't like Poppy,

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:08.438
So just play it like that.”

00:03:08.438 --> 00:03:09.522
Like, "everything you say to her,

00:03:09.522 --> 00:03:10.940
you don't like her. You like Ian.

00:03:10.940 --> 00:03:11.816
You don’t like her."

00:03:11.816 --> 00:03:13.401
And then it was just
cool to see what came out.

00:03:13.401 --> 00:03:15.403
-Dana, Dana, Dana, Dana.

00:03:15.403 --> 00:03:17.739
-What?!
-Hey, um, you just back me up.

00:03:17.739 --> 00:03:20.200
-I find it's best to, like,

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:22.202
if you approach
an actor, you kind of-

00:03:22.202 --> 00:03:23.161
you come low.

00:03:23.161 --> 00:03:24.787
-Oh my God.
-Right?

00:03:24.787 --> 00:03:26.748
You get low, and
you have a treat with you.

00:03:26.748 --> 00:03:28.291
-Mm-hmm.
-Right?

00:03:28.291 --> 00:03:30.460
And you
say, “Hey, I'm gonna...

00:03:30.460 --> 00:03:31.836
...you want? You want a little?”

00:03:31.836 --> 00:03:33.504
And then you can
say whatever you want.

00:03:33.504 --> 00:03:34.505
But you give them the treat,

00:03:34.505 --> 00:03:35.548
and you get
your hand away fast,

00:03:35.548 --> 00:03:37.091
‘cause they will bite it.

00:03:37.091 --> 00:03:37.759
And then...

00:03:37.759 --> 00:03:38.801
And then you walk away.

00:03:38.801 --> 00:03:42.513
And then, you
know, they'll usually do it.

00:03:42.513 --> 00:03:45.183
I think that was- that was-
I have found the best process.

00:03:45.183 --> 00:03:46.559
Do you guys find
that to be the case?

00:03:46.559 --> 00:03:47.352
(Snorts)

00:03:47.352 --> 00:03:48.937
(Silence)

00:03:48.937 --> 00:03:50.230
-Great meeting.

00:03:50.230 --> 00:03:51.522
-Oh, it’s ov- it’s over? Okay.

00:03:52.774 --> 00:03:54.734
So check out our
next season of Mythic Quest.

00:03:54.734 --> 00:03:57.904
And see if you can guess
who directed what episode.

00:03:58.363 --> 00:04:00.698
-Without looking at the credits first.
-Yes.

00:04:00.698 --> 00:04:03.660
(Rock music)

00:04:03.660 --> 00:04:05.078
-Being a director on a TV show,

00:04:05.078 --> 00:04:06.496
you want to get
everything that you need to get,

00:04:06.496 --> 00:04:07.455
but also...

00:04:07.830 --> 00:04:10.708
not being someone that is
keeping everyone needlessly long,

00:04:10.708 --> 00:04:11.960
and, you know, whatever.

00:04:11.960 --> 00:04:13.586
Like now.
-Like--

00:04:13.586 --> 00:04:15.004
(Laughter)

